WEBVTT

00:01:08.860 --> 00:01:10.770
WANTED: SHIROU OGAMI
SPECIES: WOLF

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:18.990
Michiru!

00:01:19.660 --> 00:01:21.910
Jackie! What are you doing here?

00:01:21.990 --> 00:01:24.330
This bread crust is delicious!

00:01:24.410 --> 00:01:28.370
It doesn't have just a brown part.
It has a white part too!

00:01:28.460 --> 00:01:30.040
You only ever knew about bread crust?

00:01:30.130 --> 00:01:32.920
It's amazing!
This bread crust is really delicious!

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:35.170
-It's a super special bread crust!
-Wow.

00:01:35.260 --> 00:01:37.590
Even the smell is different!

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:39.590
It's really delicious!

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:43.220
-Is she a friend of yours, Michiru?
-Yes.

00:01:44.060 --> 00:01:45.850
Sorry for all the ruckus she's causing.

00:01:47.350 --> 00:01:49.850
You really do make friends
wherever you go.

00:01:49.940 --> 00:01:51.980
-What?
-Silver Wolf!

00:01:52.070 --> 00:01:54.190
-Silver Wolf!
-Silver Wolf!

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:57.360
Thank you for the super bread crust!

00:01:57.450 --> 00:02:00.740
Come to the Church
any time that you're hungry.

00:02:01.240 --> 00:02:02.870
Silver Wolf!

00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:04.950
Be the best beastman you can be.

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:07.500
Be the best beastman you can be.

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:17.260
Are you sure it's all right to get
so many beastmen together at the concert?

00:02:17.840 --> 00:02:22.890
Alan said it's important that there's
a fun atmosphere like at a festival.

00:02:22.970 --> 00:02:26.140
Come to think of it, there was
a festival on the first day I was here.

00:02:27.100 --> 00:02:31.560
The concert will be broadcast live,
so I put together a list of fun songs.

00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:32.480
What do you think?

00:02:35.650 --> 00:02:37.570
What? You're going to sing this?

00:02:37.650 --> 00:02:38.530
Shouldn't I?

00:02:38.610 --> 00:02:42.030
Nazuna, you end up looking pretty ugly
when you sing this song.

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:42.950
What?

00:02:43.030 --> 00:02:45.540
And you didn't even put in that one song!

00:02:45.950 --> 00:02:49.750
Yes, I know.
It just doesn't seem right for a concert.

00:02:49.830 --> 00:02:51.120
Yes, it is!

00:02:51.210 --> 00:02:52.130
You think so?

00:02:52.210 --> 00:02:54.380
You bet it is! I want to hear you sing it!

00:03:19.990 --> 00:03:20.990
That settles it!

00:03:21.070 --> 00:03:24.320
We can't just choose the songs
that you like, Michiru!

00:03:25.910 --> 00:03:29.910
What's this "announcement" here
next to the "MC" part?

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:31.000
That?

00:03:31.410 --> 00:03:34.670
That's where I'll tell everyone
that I'm actually a human.

00:03:34.750 --> 00:03:35.590
What?

00:03:36.090 --> 00:03:38.170
Are you sure it's okay to say that?

00:03:39.010 --> 00:03:41.260
Alan said that after the drug is made,

00:03:41.340 --> 00:03:45.300
knowing that will reduce
the beastmen's stress a little.

00:03:46.220 --> 00:03:48.220
Oh, I see.

00:03:49.770 --> 00:03:52.440
Beastmen and humans
aren't really any different.

00:03:52.520 --> 00:03:54.230
We can all live the same way.

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:57.110
You and I are the ones who know that best.

00:04:15.670 --> 00:04:16.630
The ceiling!

00:04:25.930 --> 00:04:26.840
Don't move!

00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:33.180
I'll handle this!
You get back to Anima-City!

00:04:33.890 --> 00:04:35.810
Ishizaki, thank you!

00:04:41.650 --> 00:04:43.110
Are the ships ready?

00:04:43.570 --> 00:04:46.410
We can fit 1,000
on the cargo ships here now.

00:04:46.490 --> 00:04:49.450
Another 5,000 will be on
a large passenger ship within five days.

00:04:49.530 --> 00:04:52.580
We can lower the numbers,
at least for the extra from the Church.

00:04:52.950 --> 00:04:53.870
Thanks.

00:04:54.540 --> 00:04:57.380
I can't let this city disappear either.

00:04:58.380 --> 00:05:02.050
Well, who would have thought
you two would be working together?

00:05:02.630 --> 00:05:05.800
I've figured out what
the Church of the Silver Wolf is up to.

00:05:06.340 --> 00:05:08.010
Nobody asked you to do that.

00:05:08.390 --> 00:05:12.220
Taking action before anyone asks is
where the good money is.

00:05:12.310 --> 00:05:14.980
It looks like Ms. Tanuki is involved.

00:05:15.060 --> 00:05:16.730
If you don't care, I'll leave.

00:05:18.940 --> 00:05:20.230
Out with it!

00:05:20.730 --> 00:05:23.990
She was meeting with the Church founder
about a concert.

00:05:24.530 --> 00:05:27.700
They're going to tell everyone
that the founder is a human.

00:05:28.280 --> 00:05:32.660
She said that after the drug is made,
it will reduce the beastmen's stress.

00:05:33.040 --> 00:05:34.160
Are you kidding me?

00:05:39.790 --> 00:05:42.880
Say, Nazuna.
Are you really going to announce that?

00:05:43.760 --> 00:05:48.380
I told you. It's important
to help avoid Nirvasyl Syndrome.

00:05:50.850 --> 00:05:53.850
But I'm sure Shirou would be upset
if he heard that.

00:05:54.310 --> 00:05:57.480
Why? I mean,
I'm doing this for the beastmen.

00:05:57.560 --> 00:05:58.600
Why would he be angry?

00:05:59.400 --> 00:06:00.480
Yes, I guess so.

00:06:01.190 --> 00:06:02.230
Déesse Louve.

00:06:02.940 --> 00:06:04.820
We have to go now.

00:06:04.900 --> 00:06:06.440
Can't Michiru come along?

00:06:07.700 --> 00:06:09.530
People are watching.

00:06:09.610 --> 00:06:11.910
Oh, come on.
Just for today is no big deal.

00:06:11.990 --> 00:06:15.040
It's all right. There's someplace
I want to go anyway.

00:06:15.620 --> 00:06:16.540
Really?

00:06:17.750 --> 00:06:20.290
I'll make sure they know about you
at the staff entrance.

00:06:20.380 --> 00:06:22.630
-Make sure you're not late.
-Sure thing.

00:06:22.710 --> 00:06:23.800
See you later!

00:06:57.500 --> 00:07:00.500
I think there are more people now
than at that festival before.

00:07:00.580 --> 00:07:02.130
When did there become so many?

00:07:02.210 --> 00:07:03.460
<i>Michiru!</i>

00:07:03.540 --> 00:07:04.880
What?

00:07:05.460 --> 00:07:07.260
<i>Did I scare you?</i>

00:07:08.170 --> 00:07:09.090
Jem?

00:07:09.170 --> 00:07:11.220
<i>It's a Silver Wolf concert!</i>

00:07:11.300 --> 00:07:13.300
This is a real festival!

00:07:13.390 --> 00:07:15.050
Jem! Melissa!

00:07:15.560 --> 00:07:17.180
You're operating that together?

00:07:17.680 --> 00:07:20.480
We made it out of appreciation
for Silver Wolf.

00:07:21.060 --> 00:07:22.600
Until this city was built,

00:07:22.690 --> 00:07:27.320
all beastmen have suffered mental pain
and anguish we don't want to recall

00:07:27.400 --> 00:07:29.490
at least a few times.

00:07:30.780 --> 00:07:32.530
Of course, we have as well.

00:07:34.370 --> 00:07:39.910
But the legend of Silver Wolf
has helped us get through those times.

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:42.330
So we all built this together.

00:07:42.790 --> 00:07:43.710
You all did?

00:07:44.210 --> 00:07:47.670
That's right.
All the beastmen living in Anima-City!

00:07:48.170 --> 00:07:52.130
We built it to show our appreciation for
protecting us beastmen for 1,000 years.

00:07:52.220 --> 00:07:56.100
But it's hard to say
if Silver Wolf got the message though.

00:07:59.270 --> 00:08:02.390
I'm sure he understands
how everyone feels.

00:08:02.940 --> 00:08:05.770
He was probably so happy that he cried.

00:08:07.320 --> 00:08:09.190
I sure hope so.

00:08:09.980 --> 00:08:10.990
I'm certain of it!

00:08:11.490 --> 00:08:13.110
Thanks, Michiru.

00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:22.370
Michiru?

00:08:23.000 --> 00:08:23.830
Where's Michiru?

00:08:24.210 --> 00:08:26.540
It appears she hasn't arrived yet.

00:08:26.960 --> 00:08:30.510
Darn her! She's as bad about
keeping appointments as before.

00:08:32.510 --> 00:08:33.550
Where is he?

00:08:39.390 --> 00:08:40.350
Shirou...

00:08:47.650 --> 00:08:51.030
Anyway, Kuromaki's getting
the Family's people on the boats.

00:08:51.440 --> 00:08:53.570
Next, it's the people from the slum.

00:08:53.650 --> 00:08:55.700
They will do anything for money.

00:08:56.070 --> 00:09:00.830
Marie, you spread the word and get
as much of the audience out as you can.

00:09:01.410 --> 00:09:02.540
Leave it to me.

00:09:04.750 --> 00:09:06.330
Do you really need that?

00:09:06.420 --> 00:09:07.750
We can't fail.

00:09:08.710 --> 00:09:10.340
Then we'll join you.

00:09:10.750 --> 00:09:13.210
We can't let an overreaction
incite the crowd either.

00:09:13.630 --> 00:09:15.930
You handle things
just in case it gets out of hand.

00:09:16.510 --> 00:09:18.220
I'll stop the founder myself.

00:09:54.170 --> 00:09:55.170
Shirou!

00:09:56.050 --> 00:09:57.430
It's almost time.

00:09:58.010 --> 00:10:02.310
The lost masses of beastmen
are waiting for your appearance.

00:10:04.680 --> 00:10:07.850
Let's do this, Nazuna.
It's time to be the real thing!

00:10:13.610 --> 00:10:18.030
The roads around here are crawling
with cops and beastmen suppression teams.

00:10:18.820 --> 00:10:21.780
What's more, all roads to Anima-City
are blocked with checkpoints.

00:10:22.330 --> 00:10:25.290
I doubt you'll make it on foot, Mayor.

00:10:26.160 --> 00:10:28.250
Are you Pingua?

00:10:28.330 --> 00:10:31.460
That's pretty good, Mayor.
I'm surprised you knew me.

00:10:31.540 --> 00:10:32.460
CHECKPOINT

00:10:35.840 --> 00:10:37.090
Why are you here?

00:10:37.170 --> 00:10:39.260
I was listening in
on government communications

00:10:39.340 --> 00:10:41.800
when I heard there would be trouble.

00:10:42.470 --> 00:10:46.560
That piqued my interest, so I returned
and found you being pursued by humans.

00:10:46.640 --> 00:10:50.520
I can't have you kicking the bucket
before you build a cemetery for my pals.

00:10:50.600 --> 00:10:53.400
And I don't want the efforts
of Ms. Tanuki going to waste.

00:10:57.320 --> 00:10:59.780
Those are anti-beastmen mobile weapons.

00:10:59.860 --> 00:11:00.780
Weapons?

00:11:01.240 --> 00:11:02.110
That's right.

00:11:02.200 --> 00:11:05.160
I fought them during the wars
against the anti-beastmen factions.

00:11:05.240 --> 00:11:07.910
You can't be serious!
Get me to Anima-City immediately!

00:11:08.500 --> 00:11:09.830
That's the plan!

00:11:14.960 --> 00:11:16.590
So how will I handle this?

00:11:31.520 --> 00:11:32.650
Why?

00:11:33.230 --> 00:11:34.360
Shirou...

00:11:36.070 --> 00:11:37.110
Don't get in my way.

00:12:14.650 --> 00:12:16.900
I LOVE SILVER WOLF

00:12:40.340 --> 00:12:41.460
I'm sorry!

00:12:41.550 --> 00:12:43.550
I know I need to understand

00:12:44.130 --> 00:12:46.590
why you take the side
of beastmen so fiercely.

00:12:47.260 --> 00:12:49.510
I turned from a human into a beastman,

00:12:49.600 --> 00:12:52.980
so I should know very well what it's like
to lose your own identity!

00:12:53.480 --> 00:12:56.480
But I didn't understand how you felt!

00:12:57.020 --> 00:12:58.810
So I have to apologize to you!

00:13:00.780 --> 00:13:02.030
You're really something.

00:13:02.110 --> 00:13:03.900
But I've become unsure again.

00:13:04.570 --> 00:13:06.820
What in the world are you doing, Shirou?

00:13:06.910 --> 00:13:08.320
Why do you have a gun?

00:13:08.910 --> 00:13:11.160
I can't understand unless you tell me!

00:13:11.830 --> 00:13:14.000
Nazuna is my friend!

00:13:15.040 --> 00:13:17.790
Why are you trying to kill her?

00:13:19.000 --> 00:13:19.880
Why?

00:13:27.550 --> 00:13:28.590
I'm sorry.

00:13:29.090 --> 00:13:29.970
What?

00:13:30.430 --> 00:13:32.770
I don't want to hurt your friend.

00:13:32.850 --> 00:13:34.100
But this concert...

00:13:35.390 --> 00:13:38.770
No, her announcement,
I've got to stop her from making it.

00:13:39.810 --> 00:13:42.480
If the Church founder tells the beastmen
she's a human,

00:13:42.570 --> 00:13:44.780
it will trigger Nirvasyl Syndrome.

00:13:47.820 --> 00:13:49.620
When is she going to say it?

00:13:50.700 --> 00:13:52.870
Her announcement will trigger it?

00:13:53.240 --> 00:13:55.910
No doubt about it.
Beastmen are obstinate people.

00:13:56.620 --> 00:14:00.000
They're more passionate than humans
and trust more easily.

00:14:00.420 --> 00:14:03.090
If they're deceived
by something they believed in,

00:14:03.170 --> 00:14:05.380
the shock is even greater
than it is on humans.

00:14:05.970 --> 00:14:07.550
They'll become enraged for sure.

00:14:07.630 --> 00:14:10.640
Then it's the opposite
of what Alan told Nazuna.

00:14:11.220 --> 00:14:12.890
Alan knows what he's doing.

00:14:13.350 --> 00:14:15.140
What? But how come?

00:14:15.560 --> 00:14:16.390
I don't know.

00:14:16.890 --> 00:14:19.600
First, we need to stop
her announcement though.

00:14:20.190 --> 00:14:22.020
Can you convince her?

00:14:30.320 --> 00:14:32.530
She flies over the audience
during this song,

00:14:32.910 --> 00:14:35.740
then lands on the stage
on the other side and changes.

00:14:36.290 --> 00:14:38.960
-I can do it then.
-The other side, huh?

00:14:39.330 --> 00:14:41.080
I'll fly. It will be faster.

00:14:41.500 --> 00:14:42.880
Don't incite the crowd.

00:14:43.340 --> 00:14:44.840
-I'll follow you.
-Okay.

00:15:07.190 --> 00:15:08.030
Chief Inspector.

00:15:08.530 --> 00:15:12.030
Chairman Alan said
you'd surely show up here.

00:15:12.410 --> 00:15:13.240
Alan did?

00:15:13.700 --> 00:15:15.620
I'm sorry it's come to this.

00:15:16.200 --> 00:15:19.080
Chief Inspector, there's no time!
Let me through!

00:15:19.160 --> 00:15:22.290
I can't do that! You're a wanted man!

00:15:22.750 --> 00:15:25.040
I'll serve my sentence after this is over!

00:15:25.130 --> 00:15:26.550
This city is in danger now!

00:15:27.050 --> 00:15:30.010
If this concert isn't stopped,
Anima-City will be destroyed!

00:15:30.090 --> 00:15:31.220
Are you nuts?

00:15:31.630 --> 00:15:33.640
I want to protect beastmen.

00:15:33.720 --> 00:15:35.180
That's truly all I want!

00:15:35.720 --> 00:15:38.970
I'm begging you! Don't let this city
turn into a living hell!

00:15:45.110 --> 00:15:46.440
Yes! I made it in time.

00:15:50.950 --> 00:15:52.490
<i>There's a change in plans.</i>

00:15:53.070 --> 00:15:55.820
-<i>Make your announcement now.</i>
-What?

00:15:56.200 --> 00:15:59.290
<i>The audience is already</i>
<i>more worked up than expected.</i>

00:15:59.750 --> 00:16:02.750
<i>Let's make the most of this opportunity</i>
<i>and move it up.</i>

00:16:03.420 --> 00:16:04.250
All right.

00:16:05.250 --> 00:16:08.670
Everyone, are you having a good time?

00:16:09.670 --> 00:16:11.760
What?! That's not according to plan!

00:16:12.930 --> 00:16:15.760
-I'm having a great time too!
-Oh, no! This is bad!

00:16:18.970 --> 00:16:24.230
So many of you have gathered here today.

00:16:24.310 --> 00:16:27.650
Thank you so very much, everyone!

00:16:29.730 --> 00:16:31.900
Okay! Be the best beastman you can be!

00:16:31.990 --> 00:16:34.070
Be the best beastman you can be!

00:16:34.490 --> 00:16:36.820
Be the best beastman you can be!

00:16:36.910 --> 00:16:39.660
Be the best beastman you can be!

00:16:51.090 --> 00:16:52.090
Actually,

00:16:52.920 --> 00:16:56.140
there's something
that I must tell all of you today.

00:16:59.640 --> 00:17:00.600
You see...

00:17:17.240 --> 00:17:19.120
-Nazuna.
-Michiru?

00:17:19.490 --> 00:17:21.580
-Don't make the announcement!
-What?

00:17:25.660 --> 00:17:27.790
Please! Trust me!

00:17:30.500 --> 00:17:35.130
The thing
that I have to tell everyone is...

00:17:36.550 --> 00:17:41.600
my feeling of gratefulness to everyone
who built this giant Silver Wolf!

00:17:41.970 --> 00:17:43.430
Thank you!

00:17:46.690 --> 00:17:48.520
You'd better explain this later.

00:17:49.100 --> 00:17:49.980
I will.

00:17:53.690 --> 00:17:54.690
She did it.

00:18:09.080 --> 00:18:10.000
Hey!

00:18:10.080 --> 00:18:11.250
It's one of those!

00:18:16.010 --> 00:18:17.090
Ogami!

00:18:37.400 --> 00:18:38.820
Don't be deceived!

00:18:39.280 --> 00:18:42.410
That's not Silver Wolf! She's a human!

00:18:43.280 --> 00:18:44.120
Boris?

00:18:44.540 --> 00:18:46.620
She deceived me as well!

00:18:46.700 --> 00:18:50.540
She was turned into a beastman
with a drug from Sylvasta!

00:18:50.960 --> 00:18:54.340
Then she acted like she was Silver Wolf
and deceived us all!

00:18:54.920 --> 00:18:58.420
A human pretended
to be the sacred Silver Wolf!

00:19:00.130 --> 00:19:01.340
A human?

00:19:01.430 --> 00:19:03.050
Silver Wolf is a human?

00:19:03.140 --> 00:19:04.260
You must be kidding!

00:19:04.350 --> 00:19:05.260
We were deceived?

00:19:05.890 --> 00:19:09.140
She deceived us noble beastmen
and tried to control us!

00:19:09.560 --> 00:19:13.270
We've been deceived by a despicable human!

00:19:13.360 --> 00:19:16.320
We won't stand for this!

00:19:20.570 --> 00:19:22.070
This is the work of humans!

00:19:22.160 --> 00:19:24.870
Humans are trying to destroy beastmen
with their weapons!

00:20:05.280 --> 00:20:06.240
Nazuna!

00:20:08.700 --> 00:20:09.620
Thank you!

00:20:18.750 --> 00:20:20.210
It's going just as planned.

00:20:24.220 --> 00:20:26.220
Damn it! There's no end to them!

00:20:29.560 --> 00:20:30.810
Ogami!

00:20:46.570 --> 00:20:47.780
It's happening...

00:20:50.700 --> 00:20:52.160
<i>again.</i>

00:20:53.830 --> 00:20:55.000
<i>I can't save them.</i>

00:20:56.290 --> 00:20:58.500
I'm no protector of beastmen!

00:21:02.510 --> 00:21:03.590
<i>I...</i>

00:21:05.760 --> 00:21:07.180
<i>can't do a thing!</i>

00:21:09.300 --> 00:21:10.390
I...

00:21:11.560 --> 00:21:13.100
I...

00:21:20.860 --> 00:21:21.730
Shirou?

00:21:22.400 --> 00:21:23.440
Ogami!

00:21:28.490 --> 00:21:29.910
Back off, Ogami!

00:21:33.950 --> 00:21:35.870
Don't, Shirou!

00:21:40.630 --> 00:21:42.000
Shirou...

00:21:48.010 --> 00:21:49.640
Michiru!

00:22:48.360 --> 00:22:50.490
Subtitle translation by Brian Athey
